meta {
  name: 25-Mark a notification read
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/notifications/1/mark-read
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 401, 403, 404]
}

docs {
  Tapping into a notification to clear the badge. Hardcoded id 1
  here — a real client would use the id from the inbox listing.

  No "mark-all-read" endpoint, which is what consumer apps usually
  ship. As a heavy user that would matter; as Temi today not so
  much.
}
